# Sensitive Design review

CODEX_ONLY / COMMIT_AFTER_TASK YES; explicit current-user local Release A completion scope. Gate 1 and corrected Gate 2 approved by separate fresh read-only reviewers; preserved historical preflight failure and CHANGES_REQUESTED remain. No approved requirement revised by Design. Real external write requires separate exact Human target/text consent, still missing.

Design reuses cloud-only draft/cache/connector/session authority and existing grants, adds revision and one scoped publication relation. Durable claim precedes network operation; bounded shared-row-lock callback serializes revocation/rebind and uses same transaction credential access. Exact saved version/session confirmation, remote replacement preview, single claim/replay, uncertain leaf + same-version fresh retry, moderation truth and temporary fingerprint cleanup are explicit. Additive migration/disposable integration/local-only handoff; no production, worker, AI, bulk/delete or readiness promotion.

Independent reviewer must inspect meaningful security/privacy/provider/data/migration/concurrency behavior, internal consistency and spec mapping. In particular challenge lock ordering/token refresh on same connection, durable pre-network claim versus failed transaction, actor/session and time expiry fences, replay/retry leaf semantics, immutable Save behavior, provider mismatch/unknown state, and TTL cleanup. Stop Tasks/Apply until APPROVED. Reviewer may read canonical referenced sources and current code; no mutations, tests, DB/provider/browser operations. Strict OpenSpec validation PASS recorded, not reviewer execution. UI advisory OPTIONAL / NOT USED.

